      "message": "If I\u0027m follow this correctly, __tx_char_raw() in uart_buffering.c accumulates all the transmit characters.  The chip level UART TX interrupt then works off the queue by calling uart_process_output() which calls uart_write_char().  However, since we don\u0027t have interrupt, uart_process_output() is only called by uart_flush_output().\n\nThis seems like we will accumulate a lot of console output before it\u0027s flushed.  What triggers the flush under Zephyr?",
